## 2. What shipped

### 2.1 Product ooda lsp completion

  `initialize` advertises `completionProvider` with trigger `&`.
  `textDocument/completion` on `&Fs` returns `&FsCap`.
  Prefix uses line and character. No fake `"prefix"` key.
  Hover on `add` still says `fn add`. Not first-fn-only.

  Proof:

    ./bin/ooda run ./scripts/lsp_complete_smoke.oo
    -> lsp_complete_smoke: PASSED

  Live `./bin/ooda lsp` prints
  `completionProvider` and `"label":"&FsCap"`.

### 2.2 Real launch --exec

  After the gate is ok, `--exec` calls `run_oodac_run` on the
  pinned `.oo`. The old `sh -c "test -e …; exit 0"` line is gone.
  Without `--exec`, print the path only. A missing name exits 2.

  Proof:

    ./bin/ooda run ./scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo
    -> pm_launch_exec_smoke: PASSED (twice)

    ./bin/ooda launch --exec runme  -> LAUNCH_EXEC_OK
    ./bin/ooda launch runme         -> ooda launch: ok <path>
    ./bin/ooda launch --exec nosuchpkg -> exit 2, not installed

### 2.3 Real ooda bench

  `ooda bench FILE` typechecks FILE and prints wall time from
  `now_ms` under TimeCap. It does not print `ooda bench: ok`.
  No file or a missing file exits 2.

  Proof:

    ./bin/ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo
    -> ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 5ms
    second run: 6ms

    ./bin/ooda run ./scripts/bench_smoke.oo
    -> bench_smoke: PASSED

    ./bin/ooda bench                -> usage, exit 2
    ./bin/ooda bench missing_no_such.oo -> ERR, exit 2

  Help names `ooda bench <file.oo> [--run]`.
  `strings` on `bin/ooda` has no `ooda bench: ok`.

